From 75fc24e8d436aa766ab0efe2f8cdeefa9284e816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernt Budde <bernt.budde@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:47:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 64/99] Lexer: a [ or { after a dereference block or a
 key/value slice name subscripts it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a term perl expects an operator, and a [ or { there subscripts
the term: ${$r}[0] is an element of @$r, ${a}[1] of @a, @{$r}[0, 1]
an array slice, %{$r}[0, 1] and %h{'a', 'b'} key/value slices.
_square knew the [ after a symbol and after ->, but not after a
dereference block, so it made an anonymous-array Constructor; _curly
knew the { after a $ or @ dereference block and after a $ or @ symbol,
but not the % forms (5.20's key/value slices), so it made a Block.

One predicate, _deref_block (a $, @ or % cast before the block), now
serves both, and a % symbol subscripts like $ and @.  An anonymous
array after a block filehandle (print {$fh} [1]) stays a Constructor.

Regression pair 62_deref_subscript (the plans of 08_regression.t and
25_increment.t enumerate the directory).  Fixes PCL §17 and §36 in
t/ppi_bugs_pcl.t.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
